 Permission and question waits use the existing interaction/Host owners for registration, identity, decisions and cancellation. There is no ProductWork capacity queue or waiting-phase ledger. Native DSH owns child execution and resource limits.

+The Product composition projects native child delegation context through the public
+`system-prompt/assemble` seam. It reads the child's effective ApprovalService policy
+for each model request: `ask` describes the configured Host answerers and fail-closed
+behavior, while `never` describes automatic rejection. Only the named native
+`subagent:delegation` contribution is replaced; root and arbitrary Host contexts are
+preserved. This projection grants no permission and does not modify durable policy.
+
 ## 2. Permission modes

 The product supplies one of three modes to each Session. Reads and searches use the local user's access on all three modes. The first two modes apply the upstream `workspace-write` sandbox to governed file mutations and Shell processes; `full-autonomous` uses `danger-full-access`.
